#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bd42029-86e9-5df4-bd11-fc3ad18b0666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(t+3)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263043} {:answer/id #uuid "890a9e80-ec7d-5b2c-bb08-48a660464ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t+3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263044} {:answer/id #uuid "b061212c-5960-58ac-9238-4768f36e4838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(t-3)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263045} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba1db1b-b2b9-5340-85f9-b32869d8488d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t+6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263046} {:answer/id #uuid "c005bac0-0581-500e-888d-03e79a4eef6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t-6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bd42029-86e9-5df4-bd11-fc3ad18b0666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(t+3)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263043} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbca82b0-6dc7-5c5f-ae3e-dd50fd1e2c82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263042}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9a9a65a-403c-5185-b342-71bb7896bc55" :question/math-academy-id "q-113218" :question/problem "$2-\\frac{(-6)}{t}=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $2=\\frac{2}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}-\\frac{(-6)}{t}=.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $t$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1}-\\frac{(-6)}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{t}{t}\\cdot \\frac{2}{1}-\\frac{(-6)}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{2t}{t}-\\frac{(-6)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2t}{t}-\\frac{(-6)}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{2t-(-6)}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{2t+6}{t} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(t+3)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting Rational Expressions With No Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ed7d801-2e96-584d-bb2f-4bd9e4288920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(t-2)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263050} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f575b2-4dc8-576c-8c50-24a3e97abbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-2t}{(t-2)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263051} {:answer/id #uuid "399920da-3e7f-5dec-aecf-11dd7c5447e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2t-2}{(t-2)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263052} {:answer/id #uuid "15925787-6f45-5e4b-ab00-deac43d4c67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263053} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fd17ba-e11c-5b9e-9ae6-c7ee60429070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(t-2)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ed7d801-2e96-584d-bb2f-4bd9e4288920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(t-2)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263050} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a038ec0-35ac-5423-8b8c-c9f80bf760dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263049}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b53c8651-7b70-5e98-a3c4-9fffe26fc66c" :question/math-academy-id "q-3536" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{1}{t-2}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $t(t-2),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit.\n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $t-2$, and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{1}{t-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{t-2}{t-2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{t}{t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{t-2}{(t-2)t}-\\frac{t}{t(t-2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{t-2-t}{(t-2)t} & = \\\\ -\\frac{2}{(t-2)t} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362d2279-58bc-5141-9962-d8f8269396f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3+x}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263057} {:answer/id #uuid "03a74146-29cd-50c3-95cb-9064b0cbdbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-x}{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263058} {:answer/id #uuid "f5525739-78ae-5289-9200-b5bb17e90128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3-2x}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263059} {:answer/id #uuid "f708c51f-eb7b-5e1e-9644-f632b7936745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5-3x}{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263060} {:answer/id #uuid "b1431eba-7e4c-5832-ab6f-eb91f767d252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2x}{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f708c51f-eb7b-5e1e-9644-f632b7936745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5-3x}{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263060} :answer-field/id #uuid "54a315ea-ff6e-5bb7-9940-f36721f06172" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263056}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53c1e98e-1b68-51ba-b58c-a209f1eb5781" :question/math-academy-id "q-70147" :question/problem "Write $2+\\frac{3-x}{1-x}$ as a single fraction." :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $2=\\frac{2}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{3-x}{1-x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $1-x$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $1-x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{3-x}{1-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{1-x}{1-x}\\cdot \\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{3-x}{1-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-x)}{1-x}+\\frac{3-x}{1-x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(1-x)}{1-x}+\\frac{3-x}{1-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(1-x)+(3-x)}{1-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{2-2x+3-x}{1-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{5-3x}{1-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting Rational Expressions With No Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d50f41e2-80a0-5862-99eb-56af5958d76e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263064} {:answer/id #uuid "1834367f-6750-5f83-a7f7-4c472d2cb929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-2y}{(x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263065} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4a1bc4-45d8-5289-a8af-3f457aa80784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8xy+4x-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263066} {:answer/id #uuid "74c65bca-9268-5479-af2c-ecb28ae0391d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6xy+x-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263067} {:answer/id #uuid "ac889359-8e98-578c-9f27-454a63033eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+y}{(2x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d50f41e2-80a0-5862-99eb-56af5958d76e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263064} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f06b84-c61a-5544-b2a2-fbc145ba6b93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ae8d3b9-143b-5b5e-b902-d2a896c99f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-70294" :question/problem "$\\frac{4x}{2x+1}-\\frac{2y}{y+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $(2x+1)(y+1),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit. \n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $y+1,$ and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2x+1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x}{2x+1}-\\frac{2y}{y+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{y+1}{y+1}\\cdot \\frac{4x}{2x+1}-\\frac{2x+1}{2x+1}\\cdot \\frac{2y}{y+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{4x(y+1)}{(2x+1)(y+1)}-\\frac{(2x+1)2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4x(y+1)-(2x+1)2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4xy+4x-4xy-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4x-2y}{(2x+1)(y+1)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63080bb8-7a6a-505d-813a-e6c99d337064" :knowledge-point/title "Adding and Subtracting a Number and a Rational Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6edd71a-0b2f-5f67-b3d0-a1cc986dc34e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(a+1)}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263071} {:answer/id #uuid "1449c4e6-5d58-59f1-a6f6-ebdefe8c03ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(a+2)}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263072} {:answer/id #uuid "ab83a3aa-62d5-5a9c-a489-8de48df6c84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3a+2}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263073} {:answer/id #uuid "b2eab698-b4aa-556a-991e-334cede29f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3a-2}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263074} {:answer/id #uuid "2d62d85c-e29a-5d1a-bfb0-baaf28d5f750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-3a}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab83a3aa-62d5-5a9c-a489-8de48df6c84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3a+2}{a}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263073} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e99890b-e9b6-586c-83de-75b70971b01c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263070}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e424628b-d763-543f-9c9a-ead63d5c1ceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-79545" :question/problem "Write $3+\\frac{2}{a}$ as a single fraction." :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $3=\\frac{3}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{2}{a}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $a$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{2}{a} & = \\\\ \\frac{a}{a}\\cdot \\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{2}{a} & = \\\\ \\frac{3a}{a}+\\frac{2}{a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3a}{a}+\\frac{2}{a} & = \\\\ \\frac{3a+2}{a}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
